From 45a9d090694801a6ddcd0ab7c585be5b1b5f77d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:09:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] client/oci: Check the unpacked size against the image budget
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The project disk budget was only compared with the compressed layer
sizes, so a small image could unpack to gigabytes on the host.

Walk the layers first and refuse an image whose content exceeds the
budget before anything is written.

This addresses GHSA-9pvj-5r2h-r873 (CVE pending)

Signed-off-by: Stéphane Graber <stgraber@stgraber.org>
(cherry picked from commit 0b21476713ae97f4076b246e1128f77af9650f4a)
